# Frontend, project-specific

General styling lives in the focused rules: `form-inputs`, `margins-and-spacing`,
`button-spacing`, `expansion-panels`, `save-actions`, `table-row-actions`,
`list-toolbar`, `no-alert-confirm`. This file covers only what is specific to
livestream-viewer. Full reference: `docs/patterns/ui-style-guidelines.md` and
`docs/patterns/frontend-guide.md`.

## Data and state

- **Layout geometry comes from the API.** Render layout pickers and tile editors from the
  normalised rects in `GET /api/v1/layouts`. Never hard-code cell positions in CSS or
  component state. Do not hard-code the family list either — derive it from the response,
  or a family added server-side silently drops its layouts from the picker.
- **`full` is the only single-cell layout** (`FULL_BLEED_ID` in `@/utils/layouts`). The old
  `1x1` was retired as a duplicate; databases are migrated on startup.
- **Live state comes from the SSE stream** via `useEventStream()`. Never poll.
- **Build every URL through `getIngressBase()`**, including the MJPEG preview `<img src>`,
  which is easy to miss because it does not go through the API client.
- **Never distort the preview.** Render it in the output's aspect ratio with letterboxing.
- **Software decode is a `warning` chip, not `success`.** On constrained hosts it is often the difference
  between a wall that works and one that does not.

## Shared primitives — use these, do not re-implement

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Nothing-here placeholder | `components/common/EmptyState.vue` |
| Delete confirmation | `components/common/ConfirmDeleteDialog.vue` |
| Any other modal | `components/common/StandardDialog.vue` |
| Password input | `components/common/PasswordField.vue` |
| Page error / success alerts | `composables/useFeedback.js` |
| Screen or tour write body | `screenPayload` / `tourPayload` in `@/utils/payloads` |
| Fit modes, select items, name lookup | `@/utils/formatters` |
| Password policy | `@/utils/passwords` (mirrors `model.MinPasswordLength`) |

## Dirty tracking and payloads

The Save-enabled check and the request body **must** come from the same function
(`screenPayload`, `tourPayload`). Building them separately lets Save enable on one shape
and send another.

## Feedback

- Page-level alerts come from `useFeedback()`. Success is transient and auto-clears; never
  assign a success message that nothing resets.
- Alerts go **above** the content they describe, with `density="compact"` and `mb-4`.
